# CMake build trees, wherever they are put. b-ON/ and b-OFF/ were committed by
# accident in #104 -- 675 files of object code, static libraries and a
# CMakeCache.txt full of one machine's absolute paths. The three build
# directories above are the ones the scripts use, but an A/B run makes up a
# name on the spot, so ignore what CMake writes as well as where it writes it.
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CTestTestfile.cmake
cmake_install.cmake
DartConfiguration.tcl
Testing/
*.o
*.a

# Ad-hoc build directories at the repository root, which is where a one-off
# `cmake -B <name>` lands when it is run from the top of the tree.
/b-*/
/build/
/build-*/
